menu "TrueHD probe"
    config TRUEHD_PROBE_TASK_STACK_BYTES
        int "Stack of the decoding task, in bytes"
        default 131072
        help
            The decoder's frame is some 33 KB on a host (planning/truehd-parity-esp32-sinks.md), and on
            an ESP32-C6 it overran a 48 KB stack by 10 KB (a stack-protection fault, and on the
            ESP32-S3, with no such check, a silent hang). The probe reports the stack the task
            reached, and this is what it was given.

    config TRUEHD_PROBE_START_DELAY_MS
        int "Wait before the probe starts, in milliseconds"
        default 6000
        help
            The console is USB-Serial/JTAG: a host opens its port after the chip has reset, so the
            probe waits for it.

    config TRUEHD_PROBE_BISECT
        int "Print each step of the first unit's decode (1), or not (0)"
        default 0
        help
            For finding where a decoder that does not return stops.

    config TRUEHD_PROBE_TRACE
        bool "Trace the decoder's function entries and print the last ones if it does not return"
        default n
        help
            The decoder's sources are compiled with -finstrument-functions, a ring remembers the last
            sixteen functions entered, and a task on the other core prints them when the probe has
            been silent for 3 s. Resolve the addresses with addr2line on the .elf.
endmenu
